SUMMARY:Sapphic Book Club!  - July
DESCRIPTION:Queers to the Front!\nOur book club read for July is *Of Monst
 ers and Mainframes* by Barbara Truelove. “Delightful\, unhinged\, and ob
 scenely compelling.” The queer love child of pulp horror and ​classic 
 ​sci-fi\, *Of Monsters and ​Mainframes* ​is a dazzling\, heartfelt o
 dyssey that probes what it means to be one of society’s monsters—and e
 xplores the many types of friendship that make us human.\n\n++\n\nDemeter 
 just wants to do her job: shuttling humans between Earth and Alpha Centaur
 i. Unfortunately\, her passengers keep dying—and not from equipment fail
 ures\, as her AI medical system\, Steward\, would have her believe. These 
 are paranormal murders\, and they began when one nasty\, ancient vampire d
 ecided to board Demeter and kill all her humans.\n\n[Read full synopsis he
 re at The StoryGraph](https://app.thestorygraph.com/books/44ec0922-e178-4b
 9b-bd4e-679558097dc1)\n\n***\\*\\*\\****\n\nWe'll meet at **White Duck Tac
 o** in South Asheville \\(off Long Shoals Rd\\) \\|\\| Come early if you w
 ant some yummy food and drinks\\!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/queers-to-the-front/events/315647731/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260712T004846Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260712T004846Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Queers to the Front!
UID:event_315651727@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260719T042032Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260801T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260801T150000
SUMMARY:Let’s Craft!
DESCRIPTION:Queers to the Front!\nGreetings everyone! Let’s get together
  and craft while snacking on pie! You can bring whatever craft you’re in
 to\, though please don’t bring anything too big/messy (e.g. no mural pai
 nting) since we want everyone to have space to work and need to leave the 
 place spotless!\n\nThe Baked Pie Company has an ever rotating selection of
  award-winning pies (as well as quiche and salad)\; they even have pie fli
 ghts! They also feature sugar free\, gluten free\, keto and vegan pies for
  those with dietary needs. So let's grab a slice of pie and build some com
 munity!\n\nDon't worry if you can't make this one\, though! It’s a month
 ly event\; you'll have plenty of chances to get your pie on :)\n\nYou can 
 check out the menu here:\nhttps://www.bakedpiecompany.com/list-of-pies
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/queers-to-the-front/events/315651727/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260712T120401Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260712T120401Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Queers to the Front!
UID:event_315077013@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260719T042032Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T210000
SUMMARY:Everybody But You Bro Comedy Open Mic
DESCRIPTION:Queers to the Front!\nJoin Eyes Up Here Comedy & Modelface Com
 edy for the premiere open mic for the rest of us -- Everybody But You Bro 
 is a comedy mic for women\, non-binary\, queer and femme folks to take the
  stage and tell jokes -- up to 5 minutes.\n\nThis is a queer and trans-inc
 lusive mic.\nWe don’t punch down y’all!\n\nSign ups at 6pm and shows s
 tarts at 6:30pm and it’s show up and go up! Located in the Comedy Baseme
 nt at The RAD Brew Co.\nAll are welcome for the audience\, however heckler
 s will be asked to leave\n\nFree event\, Suggested $10 donations are highl
 y encouraged\nHosted by Erin Terry\, Danny Felix and Linda Barsi\nStick ar
 ound after the mic for our Joke Writing Workshop at 8pm
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/queers-to-the-front/events/315077013/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260602T222312Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260602T222312Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
